===============================================================================
8. SCHEDULED JOBS
===============================================================================

ScopeCreep backup:
    vps-backup.timer

    Schedule:
        daily at 04:15
        RandomizedDelaySec=15m
        Persistent=true

    Service:
        vps-backup.service

    Entry point:
        /usr/local/sbin/vps-backup

Clanker backup repository maintenance:
    clanker-backup-maintenance.timer

    Schedule:
        Sunday at 05:00
        RandomizedDelaySec=15m
        Persistent=true

    Service:
        clanker-backup-maintenance.service

    Entry point:
        /usr/local/sbin/clanker-backup-maintenance

Other observed timers include:
    apt-daily
    apt-daily-upgrade
    dpkg-db-backup
    logrotate
    fstrim
    e2scrub_all
    systemd-tmpfiles-clean
    beszel-agent-update

===============================================================================
9. USEFULSCRIPTS DEPLOYMENT
===============================================================================

Operational scripts are symlinked from /usr/local/sbin into the UsefulScripts
checkout owned by joyfulreaper.

ScopeCreep backup:
    /usr/local/sbin/vps-backup
        -> /home/joyfulreaper/UsefulScripts/VPS/Backup/ScopeCreep/backup.sh

Clanker repository maintenance:
    /usr/local/sbin/clanker-backup-maintenance
        -> /home/joyfulreaper/UsefulScripts/VPS/Backup/ScopeCreep/clanker-repo-maintenance.sh

This means the UsefulScripts checkout is part of the operational configuration
of ScopeCreep and should be restored/cloned before these units can work normally.

===============================================================================
10. SCOPECREEP BACKUP ARCHITECTURE
===============================================================================

ScopeCreep backs itself up to Clanker over the WireGuard network using restic.

Destination:
    rest:http://10.99.0.1:8000/scopecreep/

Restic snapshot metadata:
    host: scopecreep
    tags:
        scopecreep
        peer

Backup staging root:
    /var/lib/vps-backup/staging

The script:
    - requires root
    - prevents overlapping runs with flock
    - validates peer repository connectivity
    - stages a recovery tree
    - creates a recovery manifest
    - snapshots SQLite safely
    - sends the staged tree to Clanker using restic
    - sends success/failure notification through ntfy
    - removes staging data on exit

ntfy endpoint:
    http://10.99.0.1:5197/vps-backups

===============================================================================
11. SCOPECREEP BACKUP CONTENT
===============================================================================

The backup stages most of /etc, excluding:
    /etc/vps-backup/

Application/configuration paths explicitly included:
    /home/joyfulreaper/.ssh
    /opt/stacks
    /opt/dockge
    /opt/beszel-agent
    /var/lib/beszel-agent
    /var/lib/restic/.htpasswd

IMPORTANT:
    The Clanker restic repository beneath /var/lib/restic is intentionally NOT
    included in ScopeCreep's own backup.

Dockge SQLite:
    Source:
        /opt/dockge/data/dockge.db

    The backup script uses SQLite's .backup command and verifies the resulting
    database with PRAGMA quick_check rather than copying the live DB blindly.

Recovery manifest generated during each backup includes:
    host/platform information
    filesystems
    block devices
    IP addresses
    IPv4 routes
    IPv6 routes
    WireGuard state
    Docker containers
    Docker Compose projects
    Docker volumes
    Docker networks
    enabled systemd units
    listening sockets
    installed package versions
    root crontab
    joyfulreaper crontab

===============================================================================
12. BACKUP SECRETS / OUT-OF-BAND RECOVERY REQUIREMENTS
===============================================================================

The backup deliberately excludes /etc/vps-backup.

Important files referenced by the backup system include:

    /etc/vps-backup/peer.env
    /etc/vps-backup/peer-repository-password
    /etc/vps-backup/ntfy.env
    /etc/vps-backup/clanker-repository-password

These are secrets or secret-bearing configuration and must NOT be committed to
the public UsefulScripts repository.

Because /etc/vps-backup is excluded from ScopeCreep's peer backup, these files
must be preserved through a separate secure/out-of-band recovery mechanism.

This is a P0 restore dependency.

===============================================================================
13. CLANKER BACKUP STORAGE RESPONSIBILITY
===============================================================================

ScopeCreep hosts Clanker's peer restic repository.

Repository:
    /var/lib/restic/clanker

Authentication metadata:
    /var/lib/restic/.htpasswd

Repository password file:
    /etc/vps-backup/clanker-repository-password

Weekly maintenance performs:
    restic unlock
    restic forget --keep-within 30d --prune
    restic check

Maintenance also reports:
    repository size before maintenance
    repository size after maintenance
    ScopeCreep root free space / usage
    runtime
    success/failure through ntfy

At inventory time:
    /var/lib/restic total size: ~136 MB

===============================================================================
14. PERSISTENT APPLICATION DATA
===============================================================================

Backup-critical or rebuild-relevant paths identified:

P0 / secrets or access:
    /etc/vps-backup/*
        NOT included in ScopeCreep's own restic snapshot.
        Must be preserved separately.

    WireGuard configuration under /etc/wireguard
        Included indirectly through the /etc backup unless excluded elsewhere.

    Cloudflared configuration/credentials
        Exact location not yet inventoried.
        Review before declaring restore coverage complete.

P1 / important persistent application state:
    /var/lib/restic
        Hosts restic repository data, including Clanker's repository.

    /opt/dockge/data
        Dockge SQLite/state.

    /opt/stacks
        Compose configuration managed by Dockge.

    /opt/stacks/beszel-agent/beszel_agent_data
        Beszel agent data.

    /var/lib/beszel-agent
        Host Beszel state, if the host service remains intentional.

P2 / useful but reproducible:
    /home/joyfulreaper/UsefulScripts
        Operational source checkout.
        Re-clonable from GitHub but required for symlinked backup entry points.

Regeneratable / normally do not back up:
    /var/lib/docker
    /var/lib/containerd
    Docker images
    Docker writable layers
    Docker build cache

