===============================================================================
19. BACKUP PRIORITY MODEL
===============================================================================

P0 - required to regain access / decrypt / reconnect:
    /etc/vps-backup/*
    WireGuard private configuration
    Cloudflare tunnel credentials/configuration if ScopeCreep still depends on it
    SSH access material as appropriate

P1 - important persistent state:
    /var/lib/restic
    /opt/dockge/data
    /opt/stacks
    Beszel state if still used

P2 - useful configuration / convenience:
    UsefulScripts checkout
    package manifest
    systemd manifests
    recovery inventory
    logs needed for troubleshooting

P3 - regenerate instead:
    /var/lib/docker
    /var/lib/containerd
    Docker images/layers/cache
    package caches

===============================================================================
20. RESTORE ORDER
===============================================================================

Suggested high-level rebuild order:

1. Provision Debian 13 or a compatible successor.
2. Restore SSH/admin access.
3. Restore network configuration and WireGuard.
4. Install Docker / Docker Compose.
5. Clone UsefulScripts into:
       /home/joyfulreaper/UsefulScripts
6. Restore the out-of-band /etc/vps-backup secret files.
7. Restore /opt/stacks and /opt/dockge.
8. Restore /var/lib/restic before bringing rest-server into production use.
9. Restore Dockge database/state.
10. Recreate/start Docker Compose projects.
11. Restore/validate cloudflared if still required.
12. Restore/validate Beszel deployment after deciding which copy is canonical.
13. Enable backup and maintenance timers.
14. Verify ScopeCreep can back itself up to Clanker.
15. Verify Clanker's restic repository is readable on ScopeCreep.
16. Run restic check against the Clanker repository.
17. Verify ntfy backup notifications.

